# Force LF line endings everywhere to prevent CRLF corruption from Windows/VM sync
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files — don't touch line endings
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# Append-only closeout docs — union merge (THR-691).
# Every shipped ticket appends rows to the same table heads, so any PR that idles
# is otherwise guaranteed to conflict with the next ship in these files alone.
# `union` is a built-in git merge driver: on a conflicting hunk it keeps BOTH
# sides' lines instead of writing conflict markers. Safe here precisely because
# these files are append-only — a row is added, never edited in place.
#
# Deliberately EXCLUDES Docs/project-status.md: it has a 60-line cap and rewrite
# semantics, so union would duplicate rewritten lines rather than merge them.
#
# Applies to LOCAL `git merge` only. GitHub's server-side merge ignores this
# attribute — measured 2026-07-21 (THR-691): with these lines present on the
# base branch, the merges API returned 409 and the PR read
# `mergeable: CONFLICTING`. A docs-table PR that idles into CONFLICTING must be
# resolved by merging locally and pushing — see `.claude/skills/pull-work/SKILL.md`
# § "Closeout — resolving a conflicted closeout-docs PR".
Docs/changelog.md merge=union
Docs/project-history.md merge=union
Docs/impediments.md merge=union

# Orchestrator's per-day report — same append-only shape as above, prepending a
# new run section at the top of Docs/ops/orchestrator-YYYY-MM-DD.md every run.
# Two runs racing (this lane fires more than hourly some days) conflict at that
# same anchor otherwise — see THR-849 for a measured instance (PR #1031 sat
# OPEN/DIRTY ~18h because its sole change was to this file). Union does not
# guarantee chronological order among the appended sections on a resolved
# conflict — acceptable for an audit trace, not for anything read in order.
Docs/ops/orchestrator-*.md merge=union
